    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete. All prices now work correctly, including 39.95.\n\nThe issue was a classic floating-point precision problem. When JavaScript multiplies `39.95 * 100`, it gets `3995.0000000000005` instead of exactly `3995` due to how IEEE 754 floats work. I fixed it by adding `Math.round()` to all three places where prices are converted to cents:\n\n1. **parseEuros** in `src/money.js` - handles regular decimal format (12.99)\n2. **cellCents** in `src/money.js` - handles CSV import  \n3. **decimalCommaToCents** in `src/locale.js` - handles European decimal comma format (12,99)\n\nThe fix ensures that any price is properly rounded to a whole number of cents before validation.",
